    "algebra": "Confirmed. In the rest-volume normalization, p = −e^η U_u(−η/3)/3. At zero in-plane load U_u(0)=0, hence p_η(0)=U_uu(0)/9 and p_ηη(0)=2U_uu(0)/9−U_uuu(0)/27. For U_uu(0)>0, carrier curvature 5 requires U_uuu(0)/U_uu(0)=−9. This is a necessary local condition under the prescribed fixed-gap strain path; matching it alone does not establish the finite compression curve."
